==============================================================================================
 (E) THE Q(sqrt-3,sqrt-7) BRIDGE via sqrt21, and the residual assessment
==============================================================================================
  covering field   = Q(sqrt-3)  (Phi6 / Eisenstein / metallic-CF flavor, opus-S24)
  certification    = Q(sqrt-7)  (Gauss sum i*sqrt7, ι-odd Lefschetz, S20)
  real compositum  = Q(sqrt(3*7)) = Q(sqrt21);  sqrt-3 * sqrt-7 = -sqrt21
  deep-well D_14 = n(n-1)(n^2-n+4) = 33852 = squarefree 8463 = 21*403 => sqrt21 | sqrt(D_14): True
  => the DEEP-WELL binding CF (metallic/covering side) CONTAINS sqrt21 = the bridge of covering & cert.
  ASSESSMENT of 'is the sqrt21 bridge the OPEN-Q-108 residual?':
   - The bridge Q(sqrt-3,sqrt-7)/sqrt21 IS the residual of the LEFSCHETZ/CERTIFICATION program: the ι-odd
     Gauss certificate (sqrt-7) must interact with the Eisenstein covering (sqrt-3) to certify the WHOLE
     cover; the 'mixed' part (neither pure isotype) lives in the compositum sqrt21. Making i*sqrt7 => M>=1/n
     rigorous = bridging these two fields. So YES for the trace-formula approach's residual.
   - It is NOT the CLASSICAL multi-far census residual: those extremizers are the pentagon (Z/10)* [Q(sqrt5)]
     and the sporadic two-clash (Z/19) [Q(sqrt-19)] -- their OWN sub-apex fields, not sqrt21.
   => HONEST: sqrt21 = the certification-program residual (a promising reformulation), distinct from the
      classical census residual. The two programs meet only if the census extremizers' fields (5,19) also
      reduce to the apex compositum -- which they do NOT, so the bridge is one route, not the whole crux.
DONE.
